{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d60bc18ba4d6d74","type":"tool_result","content":"1468\t\t\t\t\t\t// trigger_count 5 would trip the lib default-3 cap; absent max_triggers\n1469\t\t\t\t\t\t// means no cap, so the routing assignee survives and no escalation section\n1470\t\t\t\t\t\t// is appended (the production incident: Daily Sentry Triage assignee strip).\n1471\t\t\t\t\t\twriteTaskFile(\n1472\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"my-task.md\",\n1473\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"---\\ntask_identifier: test-task-uuid-1234\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: planning\\ntrigger_count: 5\\nassignee: sentry-collector-agent\\n---\\n## Result\\nStatus: failed\\n\",\n1474\t\t\t\t\t\t)\n1475\t\t\t\t\t\ttaskFile = lib.Task{\n1476\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTaskIdentifier: identifier,\n1477\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFrontmatter: lib.TaskFrontmatter{\n1478\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"task_identifier\": \"test-task-uuid-1234\",\n1479\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"status\":          \"in_progress\",\n1480\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"phase\":           \"planning\",\n1481\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"trigger_count\":   5,\n1482\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"assignee\":        \"sentry-collector-agent\",\n1483\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n1484\t\t\t\t\t\t\tContent: lib.TaskContent(\"## Result\\nStatus: failed\\n\"),\n1485\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1486\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(writer.WriteResult(ctx, taskFile)).To(Succeed())\n1487\t\t\t\t\t\twritten, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(tmpDir, taskDir, \"my-task.md\"))\n1488\t\t\t\t\t\ts := string(written)\n1489\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"## Trigger Cap Escalation\"))\n1490\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).To(ContainSubstring(\"assignee: sentry-collector-agent\"))\n1491\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"previous_assignee:\"))\n1492\t\t\t\t\t},\n1493\t\t\t\t)\n1494\t\t\t})\n1495\t\n1496\t\t\tContext(\"interleaved partial update between read and write (race-fix regression)\", func() {\n1497\t\t\t\tIt(\n1498\t\t\t\t\t\"preserves a partial frontmatter update that landed between read and modify\",\n1499\t\t\t\t\tfunc() {\n1500\t\t\t\t\t\t// Initial on-disk state: task in_progress, healthcheck-style probe.\n1501\t\t\t\t\t\twriteTaskFile(\n1502\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"probe-task.md\",\n1503\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"---\\ntask_identifier: test-task-uuid-1234\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: planning\\nassignee: claude\\ntrigger_count: 1\\n---\\nProbe body\\n\",\n1504\t\t\t\t\t\t)\n1505\t\n1506\t\t\t\t\t\t// Override the BeforeEach stub for this test: simulate a partial\n1507\t\t\t\t\t\t// update from task_update_frontmatter_executor landing on disk\n1508\t\t\t\t\t\t// BETWEEN the moment AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPush would\n1509\t\t\t\t\t\t// fetch current bytes and the moment modify is invoked. We do\n1510\t\t\t\t\t\t// this by mutating the file inside the stub, before calling\n1511\t\t\t\t\t\t// modify with the freshly-re-read bytes. This is exactly what\n1512\t\t\t\t\t\t// git-rest does on a CAS retry: it re-reads from disk on each\n1513\t\t\t\t\t\t// attempt, so modify sees the interleaved write.\n1514\t\t\t\t\t\tfakeGit.AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPushStub = func(\n1515\t\t\t\t\t\t\tctx context.Context,\n1516\t\t\t\t\t\t\tabsPath string,\n1517\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmodify func([]byte) ([]byte, error),\n1518\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmessage string,\n1519\t\t\t\t\t\t) error {\n1520\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Simulate the interleaved partial update: another writer\n1521\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// (the executor) added spawn_notification: true and bumped\n1522\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// trigger_count to 2 between our initial read and the modify\n1523\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// call.\n1524\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinterleaved := \"---\\ntask_identifier: test-task-uuid-1234\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: planning\\nassignee: claude\\ntrigger_count: 2\\nspawn_notification: true\\n---\\nProbe body\\n\"\n1525\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(absPath, []byte(interleaved), 0600); err != nil { // #nosec G306 -- test helper\n1526\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n1527\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1528\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcurrent, err := os.ReadFile(absPath) // #nosec G304 -- test helper\n1529\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n1530\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n1531\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1532\t\t\t\t\t\t\tupdated, err := modify(current)\n1533\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n1534\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n1535\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1536\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn os.WriteFile(absPath, updated, 0600) // #nosec G306 -- test helper\n1537\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1538\t\n1539\t\t\t\t\t\t// Agent publishes terminal completion: status: completed, phase: done.\n1540\t\t\t\t\t\ttaskFile = lib.Task{\n1541\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTaskIdentifier: identifier,\n1542\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFrontmatter: lib.TaskFrontmatter{\n1543\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"task_identifier\": \"test-task-uuid-1234\",\n1544\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"status\":          \"completed\",\n1545\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"phase\":           \"done\",\n1546\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n1547\t\t\t\t\t\t\tContent: lib.TaskContent(\"Probe completed successfully.\\n\"),\n1548\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n1549\t\n1550\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(writer.WriteResult(ctx, taskFile)).To(Succeed())\n1551\t\n1552\t\t\t\t\t\twritten, readErr := os.ReadFile(\n1553\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfilepath.Join(tmpDir, taskDir, \"probe-task.md\"),\n1554\t\t\t\t\t\t)\n1555\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(readErr).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n1556\t\t\t\t\t\ts := string(written)\n1557\t\n1558\t\t\t\t\t\t// 1. Agent's terminal status wins over the stale-disk in_progress.\n1559\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).To(ContainSubstring(\"status: completed\"))\n1560\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).To(ContainSubstring(\"phase: done\"))\n1561\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"status: in_progress\"))\n1562\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"phase: planning\"))\n1563\t\n1564\t\t\t\t\t\t// 2. The interleaved partial update's trigger_count: 2 is preserved\n1565\t\t\t\t\t\t//    (because modifyFn re-reads fresh disk content; the stale\n1566\t\t\t\t\t\t//    snapshot from FindTaskFilePath would have written trigger_count: 1\n1567\t\t\t\t\t\t//    and dropped the bump). This is the load-bearing assertion that\n1568\t\t\t\t\t\t//    proves the race is fixed.\n1569\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).To(ContainSubstring(\"trigger_count: 2\"))\n1570\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"trigger_count: 1\"))\n1571\t\n1572\t\t\t\t\t\t// 3. New body fully replaces old body (WriteResult semantics).\n1573\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).To(ContainSubstring(\"Probe completed successfully.\"))\n1574\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(s).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"Probe body\"))\n1575\t\n1576\t\t\t\t\t\t// 4. Exactly one AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPush call.\n1577\t\t\t\t\t\tExpect(fakeGit.AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPushCallCount()).To(Equal(1))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dd1ef7ac5355a1e","session_id":"d5b7e577-b8e1-45e9-9e5a-be2299ed6cef","uuid":"25ccb5ef-1f6f-47f1-9fe5-c0d9f6ecf435","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:50:37.905Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 006"}
