{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f8b8583f911074e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: completed\n3\tspec: [005-bug-create-task-dedup-blocks-terminal-reopen]\n4\tsummary: 'Verified the terminal-reopen observability already shipped by prior prompts (unconditional glog.Infof at task_create_task_executor.go:261, reopen commit message at :231, both commit-message unit specs, design-doc terminal-status section) and added the missing ## Unreleased CHANGELOG fix: entry naming the terminal-reopen behavior'\n5\texecution_id: agent-task-controller-fieldmerge-exec-011-spec-005-reopen-observability\n6\tdark-factory-version: dev\n7\tcreated: \"2026-08-27T20:30:00Z\"\n8\tqueued: \"2026-08-27T18:44:32Z\"\n9\tstarted: \"2026-08-31T11:26:28Z\"\n10\tcompleted: \"2026-08-31T11:33:15Z\"\n11\tbranch: dark-factory/bug-create-task-dedup-blocks-terminal-reopen\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t# Reopen observability for create-task terminal reopen\n15\t\n16\t<summary>\n17\t\n18\t- A terminal reopen is now visible at default log verbosity: an unconditional INFO line names the reopened path and the prior status, so operators can see in prod logs (without raising the log level) which terminal files were re-materialized.\n19\t- The git commit message for a reopened task is distinct from a first-ever create's, so vault history makes reopens greppable at a glance.\n20\t- A first-ever create emits neither the reopen log line nor the reopen commit message — the two paths remain distinguishable in exactly the two greppable places.\n21\t- The changelog records the behavior change as a fix entry under a new Unreleased section above the current top version.\n22\t- The design doc gains the frozen terminal-status definition, so the `completed`/`aborted` rule outlives this spec.\n23\t- New unit specs assert the commit-message substring is present on the reopen path and absent on the first-ever-create path.\n24\t\n25\t</summary>\n26\t\n27\t<objective>\n28\t\n29\tMake a terminal reopen operator-greppable in exactly the two places the spec freezes: an unconditional INFO log line containing `create-task: reopening terminal task` (with the path and prior status) and a git commit message containing `reopen terminal task`, both emitted only on the reopen path that prompt 1 plumbed into the write call. Record the behavior change in the changelog and document the frozen terminal-status rule in `docs/controller-design.md`.\n30\t\n31\t</objective>\n32\t\n33\t<context>\n34\t\n35\tThere is no CLAUDE.md in this repo; the global YOLO container CLAUDE.md (already in your context) governs project conventions. Read the repo's own code as the source of truth for style.\n36\t\n37\tRead the coding-plugin docs that apply to this change:\n38\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` (entry format, `## Unreleased` placement, prefix rules)\n39\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-glog-guide.md` (unconditional `glog.Infof` vs `glog.V(n).Infof`)\n40\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md`\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md`\n42\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/definition-of-done.md`\n43\t\n44\tDEPENDENCY — verify prompt 1 shipped before changing anything:\n45\t\n46\t```\n47\tcd /workspace && grep -n 'reopened bool' pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\tThe `writeTaskFile` signature MUST now include `reopened bool, priorStatus string` (threaded from `checkTitlePathFree` by the previous prompt). If the grep returns no match, STOP and report `status: failed` with message `\"terminal-reopen plumbing not yet deployed (prompt 1)\"` — do NOT re-implement the decision or change signatures here.\n51\t\n52\tRead `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go` IN FULL, focusing on:\n53\t- `writeTaskFile(ctx, gitClient, relPath, cmd, vaultName, reopened bool, priorStatus string) error` (the function you change — after prompt 1 it already declares `reopened`/`priorStatus` but does not consume them). Current body: build content via `buildCreateTaskContent`, then `gitClient.AtomicWriteAndCommitPush(ctx, absPath, content, \"[agent-task-controller] create task \"+string(cmd.TaskIdentifier))`, then `glog.V(2).Infof(\"create-task: created task file at %s for %s\", relPath, cmd.TaskIdentifier)`.\n54\t- The handler in `NewCreateTaskExecutor` already captures `reopened, priorStatus, err := checkTitlePathFree(...)` and passes both into `writeTaskFile`.\n55\t\n56\tRead `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor_test.go` IN FULL for the Ginkgo harness (`package command_test`, `mocks.GitClient`, `buildCmdObj`, `AtomicWriteAndCommitPushArgsForCall(i int) (context.Context, string, []byte, string)` where the 4th value is the commit message, default `ReadFileReturns(nil, errors.New(\"GET file returned 404: not found\"))`).\n57\t\n58\tRead `CHANGELOG.md` — the current top version heading is `## v0.5.2`; there is no `## Unreleased` section yet. The AC evidence is a `terminal` line above the top version heading.\n59\t\n60\tRead `docs/controller-design.md` — the `## Frontmatter Merge` section (around lines 52-60) documents the status/phase merge semantics that the terminal-status definition relies on; the new terminal-status section belongs near it.\n61\t\n62\t<!-- OPEN QUESTION for the human reviewer: the spec freezes only the substrings `create-task: reopening terminal task` (log) and `reopen terminal task` (commit message). This prompt picks the full commit-message form `\"[agent-task-controller] reopen terminal task <id>\"` to mirror the existing `\"[agent-task-controller] create task <id>\"` form — confirm the prefix/suffix choice at audit. -->\n63\t\n64\t</context>\n65\t\n66\t<requirements>\n67\t\n68\t1. **Consume the reopen signal in `writeTaskFile` in `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go`.** The function already has the `reopened bool` and `priorStatus string` parameters (from the previous prompt). Change the commit message passed to `AtomicWriteAndCommitPush` from the unconditional form to a branch on `reopened`:\n69\t   ```go\n70\t   msg := \"[agent-task-controller] create task \" + string(cmd.TaskIdentifier)\n71\t   if reopened {\n72\t       msg = \"[agent-task-controller] reopen terminal task \" + string(cmd.TaskIdentifier)\n73\t   }\n74\t   ```\n75\t   The reopen message MUST contain the frozen substring `reopen terminal task` (spec Desired Behavior 5 + AC). The first-create message is unchanged.\n76\t\n77\t2. **Emit the unconditional reopen INFO log in `writeTaskFile`** after the successful `AtomicWriteAndCommitPush` and after the existing `glog.V(2).Infof(\"create-task: created task file at %s for %s\", ...)` line, gated on `reopened`:\n78\t   ```go\n79\t   if reopened {\n80\t       glog.Infof(\n81\t           \"create-task: reopening terminal task at %s (prior status %s)\",\n82\t           relPath,\n83\t           priorStatus,\n84\t       )\n85\t   }\n86\t   ```\n87\t   - The log MUST be unconditional `glog.Infof`, NOT `glog.V(n).Infof` — an in-place overwrite of vault state is rare and consequential enough to be visible at default verbosity, and the spec's Rung-3 AC greps for it in prod logs at default level (spec Constraint). It MUST contain the frozen substring `create-task: reopening terminal task` and MUST name the path and the prior status (spec DB5).\n88\t   - A first-ever create (`reopened == false`) MUST NOT emit this line.\n89\t   - `glog.Infof` is the standard glog API from `github.com/golang/glog` (already imported); `func Infof(format string, args ...any)` is exported at `glog.go:520` in glog v1.2.5 — this is this repo's first use of unconditional `glog.Infof` (the rest of the file uses `glog.V(n).Infof`), which is intentional and required.\n90\t\n91\t3. **Update the `writeTaskFile` doc comment** to state that on `reopened == true` the write emits the unconditional INFO log `create-task: reopening terminal task` and commits with a `reopen terminal task` message, and that a first-ever create carries neither.\n92\t\n93\t4. **Add the commit-message unit specs** to `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor_test.go` as a new `Context` block inside `Describe(\"NewCreateTaskExecutor\")`. Assert both directions (spec AC):\n94\t   - **Positive (reopen):** stage `fakeGit.ReadFileReturns([]byte(\"---\\ntask_identifier: old\\nassignee: alice\\nstatus: completed\\nphase: done\\n---\\nprior verdict\\n\"), nil)`; handle once; capture `_, _, _, message := fakeGit.AtomicWriteAndCommitPushArgsForCall(0)`; assert `Expect(message).To(ContainSubstring(\"reopen terminal task\"))` and `Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())`.\n95\t   - **Negative (first-ever create):** keep the `BeforeEach` default 404 read (title path free); handle once; capture the message; assert `Expect(message).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"reopen terminal task\"))` and `Expect(message).To(ContainSubstring(\"create task\"))`.\n96\t   Do NOT assert the INFO log output — the repo has no glog-capture harness; the log is verified by the frozen-substring grep in `<verification>`.\n97\t\n98\t5. **Add the CHANGELOG entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.** Per `changelog-guide.md`: add a `## Unreleased` section immediately above the current top version heading `## v0.5.2` (never above the `# Changelog` header block), with a single `fix:` bullet that names the terminal-reopen behavior change specifically (no `- fix: fix bug`). The word `terminal` MUST appear in the bullet (spec AC). Example shape:\n99\t   ```\n100\t   ## Unreleased\n101\t\n102\t   - fix: reopen terminal task title slots on create — a create-task command whose title path holds a task with status `completed` or `aborted` now materializes a fresh task at that path instead of being dropped with `ErrTaskAlreadyExists` (terminal-task reopen, spec 005)\n103\t   ```\n104\t   The `fix:` prefix drives a patch version bump on release; the release agent renames `## Unreleased` to the next version heading after merge.\n105\t\n106\t6. **Add the terminal-status definition to `docs/controller-design.md`.** Insert a new section `## Terminal Task Status (create-task dedup)` immediately after the `## Frontmatter Merge` section (around line 60). The section must state, in prose (markdown file, no Go):\n107\t   - The vault has exactly two terminal task statuses: `completed` and `aborted`.\n108\t   - `done` is a `phase` value, not a `status`, and is NOT terminal for the dedup rule (status/phase merge semantics documented in `## Frontmatter Merge`).\n109\t   - `create-task`'s dedup rule is \"the title path is occupied by a live task\": a create command whose title path holds a terminal task frees the slot and materializes a fresh non-terminal task at that path (overwrite in place; the prior instance remains recoverable via `git show <sha>~1:<path>`), while any non-terminal status or any existing file whose status cannot be read holds the path and is dropped with `ErrTaskAlreadyExists`.\n110\t   - The word `terminal` MUST appear (consistency with the changelog AC's grep target; the spec Constraint requires the definition to outlive the spec).\n111\t\n112\t7. **Self-check before finishing:** re-run the `<verification>` block and confirm it passes; walk each acceptance criterion from the spec against the change — both frozen-substring greps ≥1 line in `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go`, commit-message positive/negative unit specs, CHANGELOG AC (`grep -n 'terminal' CHANGELOG.md` returns a line above `## v0.5.2`), and `make precommit` exit 0 at repo root. The Rung-3 post-deploy AC is operator-side and is covered by the spec's Verification ladder — do NOT attempt kubectl/cluster steps in this container.\n113\t\n114\t</requirements>\n115\t\n116\t<constraints>\n117\t\n118\t- Frozen log substring: `create-task: reopening terminal task` — must appear verbatim in `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go`.\n119\t- Frozen commit-message substring: `reopen terminal task` — must appear verbatim in `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go`, only on the reopen path.\n120\t- The reopen INFO log is unconditional (`glog.Infof`, not `glog.V(n).Infof`).\n121\t- Do NOT change `checkTitlePathFree`, `NewCreateTaskExecutor`'s signature, or any other function's signature — prompt 1 already plumbed the reopen signal; this prompt only consumes it in `writeTaskFile`.\n122\t- Do NOT add a config field, env var, CRD knob, or per-producer opt-out for terminal-reopen — invariant.\n123\t- Do NOT add a new frontmatter marker on the reopened task (`reopened: true`, `reopen_count`, `supersedes`) — the git commit and the log line are the record.\n124\t- Do NOT touch the unrelated `assignee`-blanking-on-failure defect.\n125\t- Existing tests in `pkg/command/` and `pkg/gitrestclient/` must still pass; do NOT modify any `Expect(` line in the two pre-existing collision contexts.\n126\t- Per `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`: `errors.Wrapf(ctx, ...)` only — never `fmt.Errorf`, never `context.Background()` in `pkg/`.\n127\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n128\t- Do NOT run kubectl/cluster/operator commands — the container has no cluster access; the Rung-3 post-deploy AC lives in the spec's operator-executable Verification rung.\n129\t\n130\t</constraints>\n131\t\n132\t<verification>\n133\t\n134\tRun iteratively while implementing:\n135\t\n136\t```\n137\tcd /workspace && make test\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\tFrozen-substring checks (spec ACs):\n141\t\n142\t```\n143\tcd /workspace && grep -n 'reopen terminal task' pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go\n144\tcd /workspace && grep -n 'create-task: reopening terminal task' pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go\n145\t```\n146\tExpect ≥1 line from each.\n147\t\n148\tCHANGELOG AC check:\n149\t\n150\t```\n151\tcd /workspace && grep -n 'terminal' CHANGELOG.md\n152\t```\n153\tExpect ≥1 line, positioned ABOVE the `## v0.5.2` heading.\n154\t\n155\tDesign-doc check:\n156\t\n157\t```\n158\tcd /workspace && grep -n 'terminal' docs/controller-design.md\n159\t```\n160\tExpect ≥1 line.\n161\t\n162\tRun ONCE at the end:\n163\t\n164\t```\n165\tcd /workspace && make precommit\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\tExpected: exit 0; the two commit-message unit specs pass (positive reopen, negative first-create); all prompt-1 terminal-reopen specs still pass; existing create-task and supersede specs still pass.\n169\t\n170\t</verification>\n171\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dd1ef7ac5355a1e","session_id":"d5b7e577-b8e1-45e9-9e5a-be2299ed6cef","uuid":"1f754699-e1f3-467c-bce7-f1bc334d3895","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:51:06.911Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 006"}
