{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_7ec9fe890bd64bd0815eba1c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both prompt files are in the inbox with execution-order prefixes, no deliberation prose, and correct frontmatter. The task is complete.\n\n## Files created\n\n1. **`/workspace/prompts/1-spec-006-field-ownership-guard.md`** — the entire behavior change: field-ownership guard, terminal pin, widened terminal early return, guard log, single package-level declarations, all new unit specs, the carved-out test rewrite, and the CHANGELOG entry (spec ACs 1-16, 19).\n2. **`/workspace/prompts/2-spec-006-docs-frontmatter-ownership.md`** — `docs/controller-design.md` § \"Frontmatter Merge\" ownership table + terminal short-circuit note (spec ACs 17-18).\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- **Kept the spec's own 2-prompt decomposition** (matches the Sizing Guide for a single feature). Prompt 1 ships the code + changelog so a release can never cut with the fix merged and no changelog entry; prompt 2 is docs-only so the code diff stays reviewable and the doc text describes what shipped.\n- **Exported the merge helper** as `MergeFrontmatter(...) (lib.TaskFrontmatter, []GuardDecision)`. This is the load-bearing design call: `result_writer_test.go` is `package result_test` (external), so the DB 6 decision-reporting AC (assert on decision count, field, kept, rejected) is only reachable through an exported symbol. Consistent with the package already exporting `FindTaskFilePath`/`ExtractBody`. `mergeFrontmatter` has exactly one call site (`buildResultModifyFn:171`), verified by grep, so the signature change is safe.\n- **Numeric-tolerant value equality** (`frontmatterValueEqual` + `numericValue`). Verified empirically that on-disk YAML (yaml.v3) decodes `trigger_count: 3` as `int`, while the incoming payload arrives via cqrs's `json.Marshal`+`Unmarshal` (`base/base_event.go:77`, standard encoding/json, no `UseNumber`) as `float64`. Without this, every steady-state publish would log a spurious guard line, violating DB 6's \"equal values produce no log line\".\n- **Terminal pin keeps the raw on-disk status verbatim**; terminal is decided only by the normalizing `Status()` accessor vs `domain.TaskStatusCompleted`/`TaskStatusAborted` (both grep-verified in vault-cli v0.116.1). Status decisions compare normalized values, so an incoming alias (`done`) against on-disk `completed` stays silent.\n- **Carve-out rewrite** models the reset as the scanner's Empty-to-Named Reset actually performs it: `writeTaskFile` writes `trigger_count: 0` + the new assignee to disk (retaining `previous_assignee: claude`) before the second publish, instead of sending `trigger_count: 0` in the incoming payload. This is the only pre-existing test block modified; both intent assertions (`previous_assignee: claude`, `assignee: backtest-agent`) are preserved.\n- **No bare git in `<verification>`**: git is masked in this container (verified: `git status` → \"not a git repository\"), so AC 14's git-diff integrity evidence is declared audit-time (host) and the agent self-enforces it via the \"only the carved block may change\" discipline + full-suite pass. I also removed a stray `git diff --name-only` I'd initially put in prompt 2's verification.\n- **No scenario prompt**: the spec explicitly states \"NO new E2E scenario\" — every branch is reachable through the `mocks.GitClient` harness, satisfying the scenario four-condition test.\n- **Failure modes**: all rows map to requirements — non-integer on-disk counters kept verbatim (accessor reads 0, no escalation), absent/unknown on-disk status stays non-terminal, operator abort-in-flight pinned via RMW re-read, agent can't un-terminate (guard logs each publish), equal values silent, git-rest/corrupt-file error paths unchanged.\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>`\n\n- In-container coding-plugin docs: `go-glog-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `definition-of-done.md`, `changelog-guide.md` (prompt 1); none needed for prompt 2 (docs-only).\n- Project files read fully: `pkg/result/result_writer.go`, `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` (key sections incl. carved block and harness), `docs/controller-design.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `go.mod`, `Makefile.precommit`.\n\n## Open questions (for the human reviewer)\n\n- **`MergeFrontmatter` + `GuardDecision` become public package API.** The spec's DB 6 AC forces decision-reporting to be observable and the test file is external, so export is the only single-file path. If the auditor prefers keeping `mergeFrontmatter` private, the alternative is a second internal test file in `package result` — flag for audit.\n- **Numeric equality helper**: the spec didn't spell out the int/float64 divergence; I introduced `frontmatterValueEqual`/`numericValue` as a package-private helper (~15 lines) to honor DB 6. Flag if the auditor considers it over-engineered.\n- **Changelog bullet wording** is my own phrasing (must contain `trigger_count` per the AC's `awk` check, which I verified exits 1 today).\n\nSuggest: run `/audit-prompt 1-spec-006-field-ownership-guard.md` and `/audit-prompt 2-spec-006-docs-frontmatter-ownership.md` to validate before approving."}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dd1ef7ac5355a1e","session_id":"d5b7e577-b8e1-45e9-9e5a-be2299ed6cef","uuid":"8a3b200a-9415-4000-9d1d-117e52d27f0f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:03:44.587Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 006"}
