7–18).\n\n**Key decisions** (from the creator):\n- **Kept the spec's own 2-prompt decomposition** (matches the Sizing Guide for a single feature). Prompt 1 ships code + changelog so a release can never cut with the fix merged and no changelog entry; prompt 2 is docs-only so the code diff stays reviewable.\n- **Exported the merge helper** as `MergeFrontmatter(...) (lib.TaskFrontmatter, []GuardDecision)`. This is load-bearing: `result_writer_test.go` is `package result_test` (external), so the DB 6 decision-reporting AC is only reachable through an exported symbol. `mergeFrontmatter` has exactly one call site (`buildResultModifyFn:171`, grep-verified), so the signature change is safe.\n- **Numeric-tolerant value equality** (`frontmatterValueEqual` + `numericValue`): on-disk YAML decodes `trigger_count: 3` as `int`, while the incoming payload arrives via cqrs JSON round-trip as `float64`. Without this, every steady-state publish logs a spurious guard line, violating DB 6.\n- **Terminal pin keeps the raw on-disk status verbatim**; terminal is decided by the normalizing `Status()` accessor vs `domain.TaskStatusCompleted`/`TaskStatusAborted` (both grep-verified in vault-cli v0.116.1).\n- **Carve-out rewrite** models the reset the way the scanner actually performs it: `writeTaskFile` writes `trigger_count: 0` + new assignee to disk (retaining `previous_assignee: claude`) before the second publish. This is the only pre-existing test block modified.\n- **No bare git in `<verification>`**: git is masked in this container (`hideGit=true` per daemon config), so AC 14's git-diff integrity evidence is declared audit-time (host).\n- **No scenario prompt**: the spec explicitly states \"NO new E2E scenario\" — every branch is reachable through the `mocks.GitClient` harness.\n\n**Open questions** (for the human reviewer):\n- `MergeFrontmatter` + `GuardDecision` become public package API (DB 6 forces decision-reporting observable; test file is external). If the auditor prefers private