hip-guard.md` — single-digit ordering prefix `1-` for a multi-prompt spec is the documented allowed form\n> - [x] Filename reflects the primary change (the field-ownership guard)\n> - [x] `status: draft` (valid inbox status); frontmatter carries only `spec`/`status`/`created`; `spec` is a YAML array in canonical full-slug form\n>\n> ## Failure Mode Coverage\n> - [x] Spec failure-modes table rows all addressed by requirements (rows 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 covered by 8a/8b tests + Requirement 4; row 2 covered by Requirement 4's \"do not coerce\" instruction, though untested — see Recommendations; rows 8–9 unchanged-code, N/A)\n> - [x] Security section addressed: \"input validation\" (guard iterates fixed package-level declarations, never derives keys from incoming payload) and \"log safety\" (Requirement 5 names only task identifier, field, two values)\n> - [x] External calls timeout/cancellation — N/A (no new external calls; `AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPush` pre-existing)\n> - [!] New values flowing through a boundary have a contract test — **Critical gap**, see Critical Issue 1\n> - [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>` (Makefile.precommit confirms `ensure` wipes `vendor/`)\n> - [x] No cross-repo writes\n> - [x] Container-autonomous: Requirement 10 defers Rung-3 (AC 20) to the operator-side Verification ladder\n> - [x] Sibling entry points covered: `mergeFrontmatter` has a single call site (`result_writer.go:171`); the one cross-package consumer (`ClearAssigneeIfHumanReview`) is explicitly frozen in Constraints\n>\n> ## Documentation Placement\n> - [x] No inlined reusable pattern that should live in a doc — the inlined Go is load-bearing implementation matching existing patterns (Ginkgo/Gomega + `DescribeTable` precedent at `pkg/command/command_operations_test.go:21`, package-level exported helpers like `FindTaskFilePath`/`ExtractBody`, no new `fmt.Errorf`)\n> - [x] Coding plugin docs referenced in `<context>` — all verified to exist\n> - [x] Domain knowledge that outlives the prompt routed to `docs/controller-design.md` via sibling prompt 2\n>\n> ## Code Reference Verification\n> | Reference | File | Status |\n> |-----------|------|--------|\n> | `mergeFrontmatter` at ~353–364, sole call site line 171 | `pkg/result/result_writer.go` | Correct |\n> | `buildResultModifyFn` line 151 | `pkg/result/result_writer.go` | Correct |\n> | `applyRetryCounter` line 188, early return line 189 `if string(merged.Status()) == \"completed\"` | `pkg/result/result_writer.go` | Correct |\n> | `resultWriter` struct ends line 52, before `FindTaskFilePath` (line 57) — Requirement 2 insertion point | `pkg/result/result_writer.go` | Correct |\n> | `It(\"agent keys override existing keys\")` line 186 | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct |\n> | `BeforeEach` 57–105, `writeTaskFile` 111, imports `os`/`filepath`/`result` | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct |\n> | Carved block `It(\"previous_assignee persists…\")` 1351–1403; `\"trigger_count\": 0, // operator reset` at line 1389 | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct |\n> | `Context(\"trigger_count cap escalation\")` opens 999, closes 1494 (8a insertion point) | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct |\n> | `Context(\"atomic write and push error\")` at 1589 | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct (see Recommendation 1) |\n> | `Describe(\"ExtractBody\")` 1714 → closes 1747, final `})` 1748 (8c insertion point) | `pkg/result/result_writer_test.go` | Correct |\n> | `## Unreleased` line 8, first `## v` heading `## v0.6.1` line 12 | `CHANGELOG.md` | Correct; `awk` verification exits 1 today |\n> | `type TaskFrontmatter map[string]interface{}`; `Status()`, `TriggerCount()`/`RetryCount()` accept `int` and `float64` | agent module `v0.83.0` | Correct (grep-verified) |\n> | `TaskStatusCompleted`/`TaskStatusAborted`; `NormalizeTaskStatus` maps `done`→`completed` | vault-cli `v0.116.1` | Correct (grep-verified) |\n> | `domain` not yet imported in `result_writer.go`; direct require `go.mod:21` | go.mod | Correct |\n> | `glog.Infof` | glog v1.2.5 (direct dep `go.mod:22`, already used) | Low risk (not locally grep-verifiable) |\n> | `goimports-reviser` runs in `make precommit` | `Makefile.precommit:15` | Correct |\n> | `make test`/`make precommit` at repo root | Single-module repo | Correct — not multi-service |\n> | Carve-out claim that only one existing block carries differing on-disk vs incoming counter | result_writer_test.go | Correct |\n> | `Empty-to-Named Reset (spec 021)` referenced in Requirement 7 | `docs/controller-design.md:101` | Correct |\n>\n> ## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n> | Guideline | Doc | Status |\n> |-----------|-----|--------|\n> | Guard log is unconditional `glog.Infof`, never `glog.V(n)`, names only task/field/values | `go-glog-guide.md` | Compliant |\n> | No `fmt.Errorf`, no `context.Background()` in `pkg/` | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant |\n> | Ginkgo/Gomega, external test package, `DescribeTable`, coverage ≥80% | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant |\n> | No test-only package-level mutable state | `go-composition.md` | Compliant |\n> | No new interfaces → no counterfeiter requirement | — | N/A |\n>\n> ## YAGNI Pass\n> Clean pass. `controllerOwnedFields`, `terminalStatuses`, `GuardDecision`, `frontmatterValueEqual`/`numericValue`, and the widened early return are each demanded by spec DBs 4/6/7. No opt-out flag, no tunables.\n>\n> ## Critical Issues\n>\n> **1. The int/float64 steady-state equality contract (DB 6) has no test — the one boundary the prompt itself flags as load-bearing is unguarded.**\n>\n> The prompt's own `<context>` (line 52) states: the on-disk counter is YAML-decoded as `int`, the incoming counter reaches `WriteResult` after a JSON round-trip through cqrs that decodes it as `float64`, and therefore `frontmatterValueEqual` \"MUST … treat `int` and `float64` as numerically equal, or every steady-state publish would log a spurious guard line, violating DB 6.\"\n>\n> Yet no shipped test ever produces a `float64` counter value. In the test harness there is no JSON round-trip — incoming frontmatter is built directly as a Go literal (`lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"trigger_count\": 1}` → `int`). So:\n> - 8b counter rows compare on-disk YAML `int` vs incoming Go `int`;\n> - 8c's two `It`s compare `int(3)` vs `int(3)` and `int(3)` vs `int(1)`.\n>\n> If `numericValue` were deleted and `frontmatterValueEqual` reduced to `a == b`, every one of the prompt's tests would still pass, while production would emit a spurious `ownership guard kept on-disk: task … field trigger_count kept 3 rejected 3` line on every steady-state publish — a DB 6 violation and log flood. This is precisely the audit's boundary-crossing pattern (a new value crosses a serialization boundary; shape tests pass; the boundary contract fails at runtime). A cheap level-1 test is available: call `result.MergeFrontmatter` with a mixed int/float64 pair.\n>\n> **Fix** — in Requirement 8c, inside the new `Describe(\"MergeFrontmatter\", …)`, insert the following two `It` blocks after the existing second `It` (the \"reports exactly one decision …\" block ending with `Expect(decisions[0].Rejected).To(Equal(1))` and its closing `})`), before the `Describe`'s final `})`:\n>\n> ```\n> // DB 6 steady-state contract: the incoming counter arrives JSON-decoded as\n> // float64 (cqrs round-trip) while the on-disk counter is YAML-decoded int.\n> // frontmatterValueEqual's numeric normalization is the only thing preventing\n> // a spurious guard log line on every steady-state publish.\n> It(\"reports zero guard decisions when the incoming float64 counter equals the on-disk int\", func() {\n>     existing := lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"status\": \"in_progress\", \"trigger_count\": 3}\n>     incoming := lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"status\": \"in_progress\", \"trigger_count\": float64(3)}\n>     _, decisions := result.MergeFrontmatter(existing, incoming)\n>     Expect(decisions).To(HaveLen(0))\n> })\n>\n> It(\"reports one decision when the incoming float64 counter differs from the on-disk int\", func() {\n>     existing := lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"status\": \"in_progress\", \"trigger_count\": 5}\n>     incoming := lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"status\": \"in_progress\", \"trigger_count\": float64(1)}\n>     _, decisions := result.MergeFrontmatter(existing, incoming)\n>     Expect(decisions).To(HaveLen(1))\n>     Expect(decisions[0].Field).To(Equal(\"trigger_count\"))\n>     Expect(decisions[0].Kept).To(Equal(5))\n>     Expect(decisions[0].Rejected).To(Equal(float64(1)))\n> })\n> ```\n>\n> This pins the exact boundary the prompt's context warns about, with no serialization harness needed.\n>\n> ## Recommendations\n>\n> 1. **8b placement anchor is imprecise.** `Context(\"interleaved partial update between read and write (race-fix regression)\")` (lines 1496–1587) sits between `Context(\"trigger_count cap escalation\")` close (1494) and `Context(\"atomic write and push error\")` (1589). Reword to: \"place it after `Context(\"interleaved partial update …\")` closes (line 1587) and before `Context(\"atomic write and push error\")` (line 1589).\"\n> 2. **Spec failure-mode row \"On-disk counter is not an integer\" is untested.** Requirement 4 correctly instructs \"Do NOT coerce\", but no test proves a non-integer on-disk value (e.g. `trigger_count: \"3\"` or `null`) is kept verbatim. A cheap 8b table row would pin the verbatim-keep.\n> 3. **Document the widened-early-return side effect for incoming-terminal status on a non-terminal task.** The Requirement 6 widening also short-circuits when the *incoming* status is terminal on a non-terminal on-disk task (spec-mandated, Design Decision 2). One sentence noting this consequence would prevent an executor from \"fixing\" it as an unintended regression.\n> 4. **Stale comment after the rename.** `result_writer.go:200` (inside `applyRetryCounter`) says \"inherited it via mergeFrontmatter\" — stale after the rename to `MergeFrontmatter`. Executor should be told to update it.\n>\n> ## Strengths\n> - Exceptionally well-anchored: every line-number citation verified against the actual files and matches.\n> - The carve-out rewrite is logically sound — traced the second-write flow with the new guard; on-disk `trigger_count: 0` prevents the cap from re-firing and clearing `assignee: backtest-agent`, while `previous_assignee: claude` is preserved.\n> - The claim that only the carve-out carries a differing on-disk/incoming counter is true (verified by reading every counter-bearing test block).\n> - Container-autonomy is clean; AC 14 git-diff check correctly deferred to host auditor (`hideGit=true` confirmed).\n> - Sibling-coverage and YAGNI passes are clean; failure modes and Security section addressed.\n>\n> **Summary**: High-quality prompt — all code references verified, test plan maps 1:1 to ACs 1–16 and 19, carve-out sound, fully container-autonomous. **One must-fix before approval**: Requirement 8c ships no test exercising the int/float64 numeric-equality path — add the two mixed-type `It` blocks above. Note: audit-only; the prompt file was not modified.\n\n---\n\n### prompts/2-spec-006-docs-frontmatter-ownership.md\n\n> # Prompt Audit Report: Document frontmatter field-ownership contract in controller-design.md\n>\n> **File**: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-006-docs-frontmatter-ownership.md`\n> **Score**: 9/10\n> **Status**: Excellent\n>\n> ## DoD Checklist\n> - [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language (minor: see Recommendations)\n> - [x] `<objective>` states end state (2 sentences, what + why)\n> - [x] `<context>` present\n> - [x] `<requirements>` numbered and specific (5 steps, exact headers + AC strings)\n> - [x] `<constraints>` present (6 bullets, copied from spec)\n> - [x] `<verification>` present with runnable command\n> - [x] All paths repo-relative (`cd /workspace` is the container mount root)\n> - [x] No bare `git ` commands when `hideGit` is on — **`hideGit=true` is in effect** (daemon arg). The prompt con